speechtext:
This is a large item and
the Estimates for the present year are based on the expenditure of the past year. The Estimates are made up in this way: Salaries and fees, $200,000; travelling expenses, $140,000; general expenses, $15,000; printing and stationery, $5,000; dipping, $10,000. Then there is a laTge item paid each year for compensation for animals that are killed by authority of the veterinary inspectors as follows:	Glanders,	$35,000;
hog cholera, $100,000; dourine, $35,000; tuberculosis, $30,000. The amount that was spent under this item in 1915-16 was $348,287. The work of this division is limited to the control and reduction of contagious and infectious diseases governed by the Animals Contagious Diseases Act. Fortunately, the only diseases which have necessitated official action in this country are glanders, dourine, anthrax, hog cholera, mange, rabies, and tuberculosis. Any new work which this division has been called upon to perform has consisted of changes in the system of combatting diseases due to modem discoveries. Two-thirds of the cost is for animals that have been destroyed.
